CACHE MANIFEST
# playzzone-gold offline cache v11 (2026-09-29) — chains A+B (11.00-13.52) + C (9.00)
#
# v11 = NARROW-WIDTH BRAND FIX; v10 = CHAIN C ADDED. PSFree (kmeps4/PSFree, AGPL-3.0-or-later) for firmware 9.00:
# run_psfree.html plus 13 modules, rop/900.js, aio_patches.bin and goldhen.bin --
# 16 new URLs. The CACHE list below grew; the two existing chain blocks are
# byte-identical to v9. Do not reformat them.
#
# v9 = index.html changed: the launcher no longer advertises two continuous ranges.
# It now gates the activate button on the firmware actually having an offsets entry
# AND a kernel-patch blob, so 11.52 / 12.01 / 12.51 / 13.01 are refused in one second
# instead of failing after the whole cold-start ritual, and the exact supported set is
# printed on the card.
#
# v8 = index.html and sw.js changed: the launcher stops after the precache and shows
# the cold-start notice instead of launching, and the exploit runs from a later open.
# The CACHE list below is UNCHANGED. Do not reformat it.
#
# v7 = the four HTML pages changed again: every run page now carries a small
# floating log window, and chain B now ENTERS through jb.html?log=1 because
# jb.js writes nothing into #out without that param. The CACHE list below is
# UNCHANGED -- jb.html?log=1 was already listed and is now the entry point
# rather than a link target. Do not reformat it.
#
# v6 = patches/1302.bin, 1350.bin and 1352.bin replaced with the upstream "aio
# fix" blobs (632 B, previously 314 B) from raw13g/raw13g.github.io commit
# ef1670a8, credited to MODDED_WARFARE and Al-Azif. The 314 B generation those
# three replaced was byte-identical to the 314 B build still shipped as
# patches/1304.bin, so this is the same blob corrected, not a new format.
# The CACHE list was unchanged: same 3 URLs, different bytes.
# patches/1250.bin, 1300.bin and 1304.bin stay at 314 B -- upstream ships no
# fixed version of those to take.
#
# v5 = UI redesign only. index.html / jb.html / run_*.html all changed again (they
# are now bilingual ع / EN), so this comment is bumped purely to force AppCache-only
# browsers to re-validate and pick up the new markup. The CACHE list below is
# byte-identical to v4 and was already complete -- it covers all 9 patches/*.bin,
# both payloads, every module and every ?ui=3 / ?v=10 / ?log=1 variant. Do not
# reformat it.
#
# v3 = two chains in one page. The GOLD chain keeps its original filenames;
# the new chain (13.02-13.52) is stored under jb_* names so both chains can
# coexist in the same folder and in the same AppCache.
#
# RULES (learned from v1/v2 bugs):
#  1) Comments must sit on their own line and start with '#'. A '#' inside a
#     URL line is parsed as a URL fragment which invalidates every entry below.
#  2) AppCache matches URLs EXACTLY (query string included). So both forms of
#     each page/module must be listed: run_*.html and run_*.html?ui=3,
#     core.js and core.js?v=10, jb.html and jb.html?log=1, jb.js?v=10,
#     jb_core.js?jbv=10.
#  3) Bumping the comment forces AppCache to re-validate on the next online
#     visit; the CACHE list itself did not need to change for that.
#
# GOLD chain (unchanged from v2.1, plus 1302/1304 kpatches that were missing):
CACHE:
index.html
run_lapse.html
run_poops.html
run_lapse.html?ui=3
run_poops.html?ui=3
chain_lapse.js?ui=3
chain_poops.js?ui=3
core.js
core.js?v=10
mem.js
int64.js
ps4_offsets.js
rpc_worker.js
logo_playzone.png
payload.bin
patches/1100.bin
patches/1150.bin
patches/1200.bin
patches/1250.bin
patches/1300.bin
patches/1302.bin
patches/1304.bin

# CHAIN C — 9.00, PSFree (kmeps4/PSFree, AGPL-3.0-or-later). A separate project
# with its own module tree, so it shares nothing with the two chains above.
# AppCache is all-or-nothing per manifest: every URL here is downloaded the first
# time the site is opened, including the 290 KB goldhen.bin, which is already in
# the repo for the other chains and is the same file (SHA-256) as PSFree's.
# The ?ui=3 page is the entry point. rop/900.js is reached only by a DYNAMIC
# import() from module/chain.js, so it is easy to miss and fatal to omit.
#
# The .js names are not upstream's .mjs. A module script whose response lacks a
# JavaScript MIME type is refused by the browser without an error the page can
# show, and whether the host maps .mjs correctly is outside this repo's control.
# Chains A and B work here because their modules end in .js, so C does too.
run_psfree.html
run_psfree.html?ui=3
psfree.js
lapse.js
config.js
module/chain.js
module/constants.js
module/int64.js
module/mem.js
module/memtools.js
module/offset.js
module/rw.js
module/utils.js
module/view.js
rop/900.js
aio_patches.bin
goldhen.bin

# NEW chain 13.02-13.52 (jb_* renamed modules; jb.js fetches patches/ and
# payload2.bin at runtime — all listed for offline use):
jb.html
jb.html?log=1
jb.js?v=10
jb_core.js?jbv=10
jb_mem.js
jb_int64.js
jb_offsets.js
jb_rpc_worker.js
payload2.bin
patches/1350.bin
patches/1352.bin

NETWORK:
*

FALLBACK:
/ index.html